        Two unordered CategoricalIndex objects with the same set of categories
        compare equal on dtype even when the categories are listed in a
        different order. In that case their codes are not directly comparable
        (code 0 may map to different categories), so we recode ``other`` before
        delegating to the base setop implementations.
